Aws-chunked per-chunk signature comparison uses non-constant-time equality
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/argmin-security-review-2026-06-23-m2
Criticality: low/informational (attack path: low)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Fixed in 53db5320f313748428ec60e66d35cf2cf3987601.

The fix made the shared `auth::constant_time_eq` helper public and changed both aws-chunked streaming signature checks in `crates/server-http/src/http/chunked.rs` to compare the expected and claimed hex signatures with that helper instead of Rust string inequality. This covers both per-chunk signatures and signed trailer signatures.

The issue was downgraded from medium to low/informational during review. A valid seed signature is required before the chunk/trailer verifiers are reached, so practical exploitability is very low; the fix is still useful defense-in-depth and keeps all SigV4 signature comparisons on the same constant-time policy.

